## Summary

This is a Spring PetClinic-derived codebase. All the membership/owner domain logic lives under `org.springframework.samples.petclinic`. There is currently NO `fiscalYear` implementation in the main source — it exists only as a target assertion in an acceptance test (see below), while the membership number today uses a plain 2-digit calendar-year segment.

---

## 1. Membership identifier generation (year segment)

The year segment is the last two digits of the registration date's **calendar** year (`getYear() % 100`), prefixed with `-M`. It is computed in TWO places with identical logic:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** (lines 26-28) — the value returned in the API response:
```java
@Mapping(target = "membershipNumber",
    expression = "java(owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" "
        + "+ String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))")
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** (lines 19-25) — the value written to the AUDIT log:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    String membershipNumber = owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M"
            + String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
    AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} "
                    + "membershipNumber={}",
            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
            owner.getMembershipLevel(), membershipNumber);
}
```

Format documented in **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (lines 2186-2192): `'<customerCode>-M<YY>' where YY is the last two digits of the registrationDate year`, example `'LON-SMI-0007-M26'`.

---

## 2. Tenure calculation (365-day window)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** (`getMembershipPoints()`, lines 280-297). The tenure test is the `> 365` day comparison from `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()`:
```java
@Transient
public Integer getMembershipPoints() {
    int points = 0;
    if (this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank()) {
        points += 2;
    }
    if (this.namesakeCount != null && this.namesakeCount == 0) {
        points += 1;
    }
    if (this.householdSize != null && this.householdSize >= 3) {
        points += 2;
    }
    if (this.registrationDate != null
            && java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(this.registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365) {
        points += 3;
    }
    return points;
}
```
Related `getMembershipLevel()` (lines 303-316) buckets those points into levels 1-4. Documented in `openapi.yml` lines 2193-2211.

---

## 3. Business-day-adjusted registration date

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DetermineRegistrationDate.java`** — the production business-day roll-forward. Its Javadoc (lines 11-20) explicitly notes that downstream values "such as the membership number's year segment" follow from this adjusted date:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<LocalDate> registrationDate) {
    LocalDate date = request.getRegistrationDate();
    if (date == null) {
        date = LocalDate.now();
    }
    registrationDate.set(toBusinessDay(date));
}

static final Set<LocalDate> PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS = Set.of(
        LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 1),
        LocalDate.of(2026, 1, 26),
        LocalDate.of(2026, 4, 25),
        LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 25),
        LocalDate.of(2026, 12, 28));

static LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate date) {
    while (isWeekend(date) || PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS.contains(date)) {
        date = date.plusDays(1);
    }
    return date;
}

private static boolean isWeekend(LocalDate date) {
    DayOfWeek day = date.getDayOfWeek();
    return day == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY || day == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY;
}
```

The `registrationDate` field itself (persistence + accessors) is in `Owner.java` lines 66-67 and 175-181.

---

